                <pb facs="0587" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3128: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-08-06T18:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                                1924—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 7—11:05
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>158. My August 6, 3 p.m. After a conversation with the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs I am authorized to inform the Department that <pb facs="0588" n="494"
                        xml:id="pg494"/> a definite rejection of the proposed supervision is not
                    intended. The intention is only provisionally to withhold acceptance of the
                    Department’s suggestion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
